#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114884 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114885 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3668609c-7f98-53ef-8aa7-6f9c3209dfee" :question/math-academy-id "e-2478" :question/problem "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/assets/9e23d542bfc56d506f5437a35a92c304d618109ef60086e1f5a7a4fee57d8a80.png) and $u(t) = t.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114886 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbb15346-028c-59c0-9b20-cd2f408c3bcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2479" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114887 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "228ae66f-9dad-5e6d-b405-9fbe62ecb7e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2480" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6272e646-6faf-5cbf-9aa8-bfa1c9a1a5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305617} {:answer/id #uuid "61492250-b27b-5c47-b317-b118914c4bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305618} {:answer/id #uuid "41c31433-12c8-5113-bb33-8079400d618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305619} {:answer/id #uuid "12a7c4c0-521d-5b22-8f03-585838f052b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305620} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc264b1-b837-534c-ae0b-bb800191e149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fc264b1-b837-534c-ae0b-bb800191e149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305621} :answer-field/id #uuid "41aec396-46ce-51ab-bf41-4cb56972babe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e49dfe3-04a3-591e-9ea0-48737f115840" :question/math-academy-id "q-127998" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0797b573-6b49-56c7-93cc-12fbaeeb75e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327239} {:answer/id #uuid "4e904431-29ed-5d78-a761-330a0c174c0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327240} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8b39a7-1cae-57a4-9289-26e4d3651c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327241} {:answer/id #uuid "824769ec-ce6c-510e-b94f-9560539e0713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327242} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e92e6a-2135-5cd0-a91b-8edc3a4b35c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824769ec-ce6c-510e-b94f-9560539e0713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327242} :answer-field/id #uuid "929b3455-9798-5808-8dad-51b1754cf022" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed124114-d5b6-5cba-b3bb-b981a963c3d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128473" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7bf0574-f62a-50b0-b258-2bfc1dfc7afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3}+2t,\\,4{t}^{2}+6{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327246} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7bb0f9-8241-59dc-84ef-242b9967874d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327247} {:answer/id #uuid "81115a2c-3ebf-5dbb-8c65-2bfdae0f1bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327248} {:answer/id #uuid "307dc8bb-869b-5538-9834-e9edbffc46d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327249} {:answer/id #uuid "2426cc07-f1a0-516d-bfd0-c142e3b4a6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81115a2c-3ebf-5dbb-8c65-2bfdae0f1bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327248} :answer-field/id #uuid "17609dc3-c229-5ca9-8caa-b4da3800c4cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffb6e1fe-344f-5ac5-bc61-6cb251c0c574" :question/math-academy-id "q-128481" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩+2⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,6{t}^{3},\\,2t+4{t}^{2}⟩+⟨8\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,2t+2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3795bac1-857b-518c-bb87-0f04772d63f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327253} {:answer/id #uuid "2da29843-29bb-54cc-ac1f-9be3591a066b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3-t \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327254} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe3c480-3582-5a41-8f2f-d396e40624f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(1-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327255} {:answer/id #uuid "85a08aef-cfd5-5ea6-a8e9-6fb25e5de8d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327256} {:answer/id #uuid "43916381-84af-5a12-a29c-6705c4b89b22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3795bac1-857b-518c-bb87-0f04772d63f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327253} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4eb602-aa87-5d90-bc1f-726d713a57a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b0680d9-f905-5e2d-ad7e-963cf0c87370" :question/math-academy-id "q-128488" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{-t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})=-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}-{t}^{3}{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e8e5dda-2d9f-58c9-80ea-e60157e0e87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327260} {:answer/id #uuid "207b0ccc-c099-544a-ad48-4aec987a64d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327261} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b3d41f-2718-5e62-9a51-1176b24f19a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{sec}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327262} {:answer/id #uuid "6d508997-e8d0-5eb1-a25e-9c3cd228db95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327263} {:answer/id #uuid "b3fddfcd-9883-5c9f-83a3-930ff7e1a81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d508997-e8d0-5eb1-a25e-9c3cd228db95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327263} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d757322-156c-5ffd-ade3-62bd6adc4b46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9d380bc-946d-5cb2-b6f8-b82e7bbd040b" :question/math-academy-id "q-128563" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2u,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡u⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{2},$ then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,\\frac{1}{u},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u(t)),\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡(u(t))⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1688504-491d-5ed1-977d-71a2be217a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305645} {:answer/id #uuid "83e2f4cf-588a-592d-9565-6a6c5ef07e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305646} {:answer/id #uuid "eb1bba33-58b4-5a00-b06a-ff91a11fd24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305647} {:answer/id #uuid "4e255fc7-6272-5f92-82e3-d5da680cb14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305648} {:answer/id #uuid "c3894f94-e78d-54bc-9274-7c41774f70f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb1bba33-58b4-5a00-b06a-ff91a11fd24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305647} :answer-field/id #uuid "00777e8c-8742-506c-8fd2-c313410fdbd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00ec801b-e22a-5c19-899f-45b6911ab4a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128570" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34c326b2-379c-58e4-9c46-1d84ba590236" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327267} {:answer/id #uuid "e2211f80-7e5b-5b68-8324-e2084aab0199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-2,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327268} {:answer/id #uuid "d2533ed3-ca3e-5c4a-8589-11aadbd79d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327269} {:answer/id #uuid "26ab7f96-88f6-54e0-b263-a0b991bfc789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{t+1},\\,2,\\,4{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327270} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9019b2-da71-5f36-8636-4afcae9478e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,-3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2533ed3-ca3e-5c4a-8589-11aadbd79d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327269} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca83f0bf-318a-545b-be68-7cadefbf726e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "024e2103-5c9c-588b-958c-f18d46a16350" :question/math-academy-id "q-128894" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{e}^{2t}⟩$ and $v(t)={e}^{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩+{e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩+⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d01425f-3b70-574c-a92d-20751f2ee490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2}\\sin t - 4t\\cos t \\\\ 6t^{2} - 16t \\\\ 5^{t}t^{2}\\ln 5 + 5^{t} \\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113451} {:answer/id #uuid "b090149b-5ef6-5d8b-a0ce-d61e362bdfc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2}\\cos t + 2t\\sin t \\\\ 12t^{2} + 36 \\\\ 5^{t}t^{2}\\ln 5 + 5^{t} \\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113452} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4c3dce-bf0c-593a-abba-46d70e33fbe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2}\\cos t + 2t\\sin t \\\\ 6t^{2} - 16t \\\\ 5^{t} + \\ln 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113453} {:answer/id #uuid "effb43f7-ec6d-5e08-81a7-5e7e36be2e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2}\\cos t + 2t\\sin t \\\\ 6t^{2} - 16t \\\\ 5^{t}t^{2}\\ln 5 + 5^{t} \\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113454} {:answer/id #uuid "04fc473d-596e-525d-a704-71e09f4bf7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2}\\cos t + 2t\\sin t \\\\ t^{2} - t \\\\ 5^{t} + 5^{t} \\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "effb43f7-ec6d-5e08-81a7-5e7e36be2e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2}\\cos t + 2t\\sin t \\\\ 6t^{2} - 16t \\\\ 5^{t}t^{2}\\ln 5 + 5^{t} \\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113454} :answer-field/id #uuid "59225c10-9e1e-5bf1-bb3a-9e5070bd56bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39b28ff1-22a5-53af-8f2d-4d751a5c5d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-32286" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({5}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+2t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2{t}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95efbad6-b565-586c-bc8c-e346736b1125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327274} {:answer/id #uuid "c6099b29-cb16-5f47-ae26-faa61bf4b759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327275} {:answer/id #uuid "00a96291-62d0-5490-b5c7-976b882ec7aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327276} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d7e36f-f584-5952-9e24-f1423ecac285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327277} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc39652-a88b-5eee-bd56-943a70c8d6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2d7e36f-f584-5952-9e24-f1423ecac285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327277} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d6bd355-3ffb-5e9d-b726-0ca182b67512" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c3942f9-741e-500b-b021-a56f2876f5b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-32499" :question/problem "Differentiate $2g(t)-h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t-3,\\,-{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-t,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have\n\n$$\n(2g(t)-h(t))^{′}=2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2g(t)-h(t))^{′} & =2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6-(-1),\\,-4t-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef7085ac-a6ae-51cf-8d34-b9fde3ec025a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327281} {:answer/id #uuid "bd21e7c5-8371-5b75-8447-6ce7fe86eca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t\\,i+8t\\,j+12t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327282} {:answer/id #uuid "a9586f72-890c-5b16-a110-d043b18b3118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}i+2{t}^{2}\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327283} {:answer/id #uuid "5a880e73-be30-5a64-a543-3b4a53489a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327284} {:answer/id #uuid "c63cb60e-a89b-5537-8df8-b692d3b4c1cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t\\,i+4t\\,j+4t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef7085ac-a6ae-51cf-8d34-b9fde3ec025a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327281} :answer-field/id #uuid "93bb2d7f-92d2-50a3-959c-881a10527c50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af028eae-58a8-55ac-b5bf-34af76194260" :question/math-academy-id "q-32502" :question/problem "If  $f(u)=u\\,i+2u\\,j+3u\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}u\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}2u\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}3u\\,k \\\\  & =i+2\\,j+3\\,k \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j+3\\,k)2t \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cebd29e4-87cb-572b-af0f-e2f507cdff45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305673} {:answer/id #uuid "86b9e636-95ff-5f96-96da-479f305b5e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305674} {:answer/id #uuid "95fe6746-9e7e-5186-8569-90337a4cf20b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305675} {:answer/id #uuid "33425daf-de81-52c8-a41e-ea1040b0a9d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305676} {:answer/id #uuid "aa876634-6b62-550b-b0a0-cf726acb311d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b9e636-95ff-5f96-96da-479f305b5e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305674} :answer-field/id #uuid "23a8d32d-d998-5d9c-8f0b-312896fbb02c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8795bddd-70ad-516e-a9a3-68891cf5e70d" :question/math-academy-id "q-32503" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7de1e558-d278-55f6-a981-93ca06dd7f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327288} {:answer/id #uuid "37fa1e0b-f43b-5001-9551-b4528c7a34c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327289} {:answer/id #uuid "cf39db88-b32f-585b-b8b8-ccf646e5f791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327290} {:answer/id #uuid "2c642803-2513-50f8-af08-4542983f40c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327291} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0b6a77-ee0b-5d5d-8710-bf67b9e717f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7de1e558-d278-55f6-a981-93ca06dd7f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327288} :answer-field/id #uuid "66ee22d6-224d-513e-9288-ec735a3c0376" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ac3cd05-f3fc-5ed1-8ce7-9ba2fec9c762" :question/math-academy-id "q-32804" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=2{t}^{3}\\,i-2t\\,j+(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k$, find $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+5\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10t)\\,k \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2t\\,i+(0)j+(10)\\,k \\\\  & =12t\\,i+10\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(12t\\,i+10\\,k)\\cdot (2{t}^{3}\\,i-2t\\,j+(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k)+(6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k)\\cdot (6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k) \\\\  & =(12t\\cdot 2{t}^{3}+0\\cdot (-2t)+10\\cdot (1+5{t}^{2}))+((6{t}^{2})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(10t)^{2}) \\\\  & =24{t}^{4}+0+10+50{t}^{2}+36{t}^{4}+4+100{t}^{2} \\\\  & =60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dde70b3-d130-59a9-a704-074c530476f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327295} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed1e6f4-9567-5244-9885-b1048253c420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327296} {:answer/id #uuid "b330afeb-f1c7-5275-92b8-d385cc4ad314" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327297} {:answer/id #uuid "3009bed0-7929-5409-838e-291b41a616e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327298} {:answer/id #uuid "284c53b5-8f19-53d1-99a1-965543e8c747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "284c53b5-8f19-53d1-99a1-965543e8c747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327299} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f20dab2-6173-51e0-b5f6-4e6d3f417c49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e434471-9049-548d-a35e-123fe4871bee" :question/math-academy-id "q-32835" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,2t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$, find $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write: \n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,6t⟩\\cdot ⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,2t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩+⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =(2\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1)+0\\cdot (2t)+6t\\cdot ({t}^{3}-1))+((2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(3{t}^{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2+0+6{t}^{4}-6t+4{t}^{2}+4+9{t}^{4} \\\\  & =15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9c161ff-a01d-5249-9ba4-673b0b6a353b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+8{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327302} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2c20d2-f738-50da-94f6-971d9f7901b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327303} {:answer/id #uuid "94cf379d-a3bd-584f-9e63-5d3fc1e779ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327304} {:answer/id #uuid "afa25a13-13f3-54e6-9083-587d5159b115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2+2t\\,,\\,-6t+8{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327305} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3e617b-d986-50f9-9d49-60c355c307eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94cf379d-a3bd-584f-9e63-5d3fc1e779ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327304} :answer-field/id #uuid "067c9103-0d8e-5bff-a030-3cb37846f77b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d806e973-4767-5c33-a683-2e2483aec09e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32836" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨1-{t}^{2}\\,,\\,1-{t}^{3}\\,,\\,1-t⟩$, find $({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\times f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\times {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t\\,,\\,-3{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{2})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\,,\\,-6t\\,,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t)\\times f(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6t \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {f}^{′}(t)\\times {f}^{′}(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2t & -1 \\\\ -2t & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2t & -3{t}^{2} \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t) & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩+⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ad5265-3598-5d78-89e8-11be85559bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin t^{3}i - 6t^{3}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113511} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c943e7-c643-5830-b7a7-431dbe4f9e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin ui - 2uj" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113512} {:answer/id #uuid "05c9038e-40e1-54ac-919b-0d4ed8b16c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t^{2}\\sin t^{3}i - 6t^{5}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113513} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdf2e19-709a-5cbc-9e51-83b3e3047823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin 3t^{2}i - 6t^{2}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113514} {:answer/id #uuid "79e166cd-cbba-5313-b026-fe7cfa6d6c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t^{2}\\sin t^{3}i - 2t^{5}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05c9038e-40e1-54ac-919b-0d4ed8b16c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t^{2}\\sin t^{3}i - 6t^{5}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113513} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8e56878-8efb-5622-a091-91a1f8e75ff1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d41b7e5-385e-5e64-81bc-3cb7a2474527" :question/math-academy-id "q-32866" :question/problem "If $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,i+(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+12\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(12)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t))\\,i-2(u(t))\\,j)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-2({t}^{3})\\,j)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e6f936-424e-5183-99e0-988712a9e068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327308} {:answer/id #uuid "dd050266-1870-5f15-86d6-f057084932d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327309} {:answer/id #uuid "43282c4f-790d-5cd6-8f5c-5659619f19d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327310} {:answer/id #uuid "0316b704-1192-5729-b51c-e89f67f5927d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327311} {:answer/id #uuid "ce59a7ac-bc7f-5eba-9140-a5898f3e51be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43282c4f-790d-5cd6-8f5c-5659619f19d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327310} :answer-field/id #uuid "a97f65b0-6b8d-55ab-80d3-18a5b299a6ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17db3926-f364-5101-a69e-c1d34df6ed10" :question/math-academy-id "q-33122" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52709d2e-d294-581f-9d56-484236a58193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327315} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7b3206-5983-5b63-b254-e0498df9e1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327316} {:answer/id #uuid "197016fb-2543-5ac0-b838-de273370b5ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327317} {:answer/id #uuid "f39c95bd-809f-5cd9-b776-655b7a49c1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327318} {:answer/id #uuid "5623d412-2fd6-52d0-a119-3ce764edaa99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f39c95bd-809f-5cd9-b776-655b7a49c1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327318} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c645193-93f7-59fd-9b5c-fe06f6304120" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f8271aa-2e12-5068-81a4-7f21907bc217" :question/math-academy-id "q-33123" :question/problem "Differentiate $2f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,(j-\\,k) \\\\ g(t) & =(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}1\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)+3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64a0a43f-3b9f-5f8c-9f84-12d03178410f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327322} {:answer/id #uuid "b67cd514-5d5b-5d26-a442-dc0a758efd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327323} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2a9f7c-05cf-55be-8894-f40cc879a7bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{2}^{t},\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327324} {:answer/id #uuid "6916f06b-5480-5608-a66d-48411b7564d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327325} {:answer/id #uuid "d26b33c4-f4dd-5a63-8fd1-2e4e42c63241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d26b33c4-f4dd-5a63-8fd1-2e4e42c63241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327326} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf695ad-3e17-535e-b5ef-925f18c49390" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ab16987-2b95-50b0-9362-48aafca307ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-33446" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩$ and $v(t)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{2t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}})=-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩-⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7b55457-c9f9-5d0c-a7e9-237db15ce839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327329} {:answer/id #uuid "2f64baa6-ed0b-583d-a7b4-3b54733334ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327330} {:answer/id #uuid "23d3cbec-6609-5443-aa68-9e52f77ae151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327331} {:answer/id #uuid "03f1ed98-54a0-5162-a056-4a21bf99c171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ {e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327332} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2e139-02bf-500e-a4d6-71101d952c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2e139-02bf-500e-a4d6-71101d952c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327333} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccdcf9ec-f301-5cf0-88ef-a2e67a7aa2a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c43762c8-310f-5f86-a903-48bba629edc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70695" :question/problem "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {u}^{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡u\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 3{u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ 3(u(t))^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u(t)}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3({e}^{t})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "611ca792-d600-5e6f-99a1-3a89dd0cde64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305722} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba29446-9aa3-5adf-a382-bb1b9ff76751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305723} {:answer/id #uuid "14784451-5ea7-55a7-b322-97172ecb01e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305724} {:answer/id #uuid "a372e0b5-6844-5cdf-a406-2261db425471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305725} {:answer/id #uuid "b531760c-4b94-52f4-8341-0dbfbb12cd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b531760c-4b94-52f4-8341-0dbfbb12cd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305726} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a4f43c-f2c7-554a-9b2f-7a24129f32d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de33fa52-4e1e-55d5-aa30-80045075815d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71225" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
